 product or  service that people want  so this book was really good and i know  it's really good because it sold  thousands of copies across the world  and after i published this on amazon i  started getting people reach out to me  and saying  you know this really helped me this  really opened up my eyes and through  bible college and after i wrote this  book  i launched a christian business network  now i launched this at the back end of  2013  we had our very first official meeting  in 2014 january  and it was called training kings you  can't serve god  and woman but you can serve  god through money the kingdom is in our  hearts  and training kings was something where i  was i had my own business i was making  money  that's all good but training kings was a  network  where i wanted to teach people and  inspire and equip people  that had good hearts that were good  people and it was it was set up for  christians because a lot of christians  didn't understand money  and they didn't understand the  difference between being a good person a  generous person and actually making  money so i set it up initially for  christians training kings now it wasn't  exclusive we never  said you have to be a christian but it  was set up for people  generally within churches but we did  have muslims we had sikhs we had  jews we had all kinds of we had people  that were completely  atheists that would come along because  they believed in the general cause of of  what we were doing  now training kings really took off and i  ended up employing people  we had 14 different branches across  across the country  and that ran for five years and from  training kings what i found was a lot of  people started saying to me you know can  you teach me about property specifically  and that's a long story but that's when  i then set up in 2016. i set up my  property training company but all  through this period  of running training kings of speaking at  churches  um even even amanda okay when i first  met my wife we met at a christian church  and her dad was quite a traditional  zimbabwean guy he actually lived in  zimbabwe at the time so there was  a real culture difference me being from  england me being  white my wife being black being from  zimbabwe there was some culture  differences  and you know amanda's dad was a little  bit unsure  but it was actually the fact that when i  said to him listen you know we are one  in  christ and that i think it was really  that that brought real unity and a sense  of understanding  me and my wife we started going to  mosaic church in coventry  and pastor gary spicer and pastor helen  spicer  really kind of mentored us and they  still do today i'd still say my  my spiritual home is mosaic church and  coventry despite attending  one more local to my home now in  buckinghamshire but that's my story of  my faith so  when i started then doing property  training events  it's kind of no surprise that i would  say to people i would just mention that  i'm a christian  and my faith would come out a little bit  now again as i say not in a preachy way  when i'm running  property training i'm there to teach  people about property but  it's no surprise that sometimes it  spills out or people can see or i might  say your thing or part of my story  and as my property training really grew  and suddenly when i'm like having a  thousand people or week  crash courses there were some people  that maybe  a few people that might have been a  little bit ticked off but not many you  know very very very few i think it's  more the media  kind of taking the mickey out of it  because the way that i mention my faith  is in my opinion is very unjudgmental  and i think what people don't like is  people don't like it when you judge them  but that's the case  that's not just if you're a christian  that's if you're a vegan or if you're  whatever you believe in your lifestyle  choices the problem happens when you  start judging people  but i don't believe 